# Overview

CX processes a pipeline of commands which transform tabular data.

A pipeline's commands are separated by "`//`" -- mnemonic: Unix shell pipe "`|`".

Some commands have pipelines arguments delimited by "`{{`" and "`}}`".

# Installation

```
# Install ruby, then:
$ git clone https://github.com/kstephens/cx.git
$ cd cx
$ bundle exec rake install
```

# Options

   Syntax           | Semantic 
--------------------|--------------------------------
`--FLAG`            | Enable.
`--no-FLAG`         | Disable (false).
`--OPTION=VALUE`    | Sets option.
`--`                | Terminates all option parsing.

# Arguments

Some commands take one or more column arguments:

    Syntax              | Semantic
------------------------|--------------------------------
`COLUMN`                | Name or index.
`COLUMN:-`              | Reverse order or removal.
`COLUMN:+`              | Forward order or addition.
`COLUMN:!`              | Negation.
`COLUMN:arg1;arg2...`   | Processing arguments.
`COLUMN:opt1=val1;...`  | Processing options.

For most commands, all columns are processed when column arguments are given.

The column name  `"*"` implies all columns.

# Global Options

  Syntax            | Semantic
--------------------|-------------------------
`--debug`           | Enable debugging info.
`--verbose`         | Enable verbose info.  
`--help`            | Print this document.    

# Commands

<% commands.each do | c | %>
<%# log.info "command #{c.name} : #{c.examples.size} examples" %>
## `<%= c.name %>`

`<%= c.name %>` \
<% unless c.options.empty? %>
 *[* \
<% c.options.each do |o| %>
<%= code(o.brief) %> \
<% end %> \
 *]* \
<% end %> \
<% c.arguments.each do |n| %>
<%= code(n) %> \
<% end %> \
<% if c.has_column_args? %>
*[* *column-args *...* *]* \
<% end %> \
<% if c.has_pipeline_args? %> \
*[* `{{` *pipeline* `}}` *...* *]* \
<% end %>

<%= c.synopsis %>

<% unless c.aliases.empty? %>
Aliases: <%= c.aliases.map{|x| code x}.join(', ') %>
<% end %>

<% unless c.options.empty? %>
  Options                   |  Description
----------------------------|------------------------------- \
<% c.options.each do | o | %>
<%= code(o.brief) %> | <%= o.description %> \
<% end %>
<% end %>

<%= c.description unless c.description.empty? %>

<% unless c.examples.empty? %>
  Examples:

<% c.examples.each do | e | %>
```
$ <%= e.example %>
<%= e.contents.actual %>```
<% end # examples.each %>
<% end # unless c.examples.empty? %>

<% end # commands %>

